WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.342
DARTFormer builds a single-layer supernetwork that
holds one candidate block for every

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:07.674
efficient attention type in parallel.

00:00:07.754 --> 00:00:12.213
Borrowing the fixed-alpha trick from differentiable
architecture search,

00:00:12.293 --> 00:00:16.690
it does not learn softmax edge weights and skips
bi-level optimization;

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:20.157
instead it simply averages the candidate block outputs,

00:00:20.237 --> 00:00:24.003
which lets the supernetwork train all the way to
convergence.

00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:25.453
To rank the attentions,

00:00:25.533 --> 00:00:29.803
it uses a masked validation accuracy drop metric:
mask out one block,

00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:32.450
measure how far validation accuracy falls,

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.359
and the block whose removal hurts the most is
judged the best.

00:00:36.439 --> 00:00:41.340
For homogeneous models the top-scoring block is
chosen; for heterogeneous ones,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.744
blocks are either pruned worst-first with fine-tuning,

00:00:44.824 --> 00:00:49.220
or the top four are taken directly and stacked into
a full Transformer.
